{"skill":{"slug":"subagent-driven-development","displayName":"Subagent Driven Development"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1770691921766,"changelog":"Initial release: 子代理驱动开发","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":9976,"sha256":"994b89a5d294eadd6a1611edb51377bac748d5f5fb7f4139d3c736b616b3a46a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"code-quality-reviewer-prompt.md","size":630,"sha256":"11de35dba7990f9def49b90039f1f2d8e7f546ae42ca8e1105d308f09456803e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"implementer-prompt.md","size":2195,"sha256":"9740dc8e425f9e1d6dc34599e0ba82e93aad7fedbcbb27b0bd67a4fa0e15a85e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"spec-reviewer-prompt.md","size":1999,"sha256":"631980e472eec5394de8b89b69d432e54fd3f7f523ecf9afa7eb4cda0c9b2baf","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2039,"sha256":"a5e155606cac323d72f8e7f8e051037c9b969f308831e299817993779b666f44","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789056694125,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"412a90b476a7c45e3033a1b671c00c1496757290ba34e876e4e1d44499144d88","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/412a90b476a7c45e3033a1b671c00c1496757290ba34e876e4e1d44499144d88","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: subagent-driven-development\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThis skill bundle outlines a multi-agent development workflow with strong emphasis on quality assurance and security best practices. Key indicators for benign classification include explicit instructions in `SKILL.md` to 'Never' perform risky actions (e.g., work on main branch, skip reviews) and to use isolated workspaces (`superpowers:using-git-worktrees`). Furthermore, `spec-reviewer-prompt.md` contains critical instructions for the reviewer subagent to 'DO NOT TRUST' the implementer's report and to independently verify code, actively mitigating potential prompt injection or misrepresentation from other agents. No evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence, or obfuscation was found.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162654778},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":15,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789056694125},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed development workflow for using subagents to implement, test, review, and commit planned code changes in an isolated workspace.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Repository file reads, tests, commits, and subagent reviews are proportionate for a development-plan execution skill; no credential access, broad indexing, network exfiltration, or unrelated system access was identified.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact contains Markdown skill and prompt templates only; no executable install script, packaged code, remote payload retrieval, or dependency installation was found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The workflow intentionally mutates repository state and can proceed across multiple tasks, but it scopes work to a provided plan, says to use one implementer at a time, requires review gates, and tells the agent not to start on main/master without explicit user consent.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No cron jobs, startup hooks, services, cross-session state files, privilege escalation, or persistent background workers were present; TodoWrite is used as session task tracking in the described workflow.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is executing implementation plans with independent tasks, and the described capabilities match that purpose: per-task implementer subagents, spec review, code quality review, testing, and commits.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want an agent to carry out a full implementation plan in your repository, including file changes, tests, reviews, and commits. Start from an isolated worktree or non-main branch and make commit permission explicit before invoking the workflow.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The skill does instruct implementation subagents to edit, test, and commit code, which is expected for this workflow and is disclosed in both the process and implementer prompt; users should still confirm the target repo, branch/worktree, and commit permission before use.\n[RA2] unexpected: The cited text refers to creating TodoWrite task entries and calling a finishing workflow skill, not to cron jobs, startup scripts, durable state, or unauthorized session persistence.\n[aig-skill-scan] expected: The static scan reported no security results, consistent with inspection of the Markdown-only artifact.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789056694125}}}}}